 "text": "Let's unpack this. We've got a fantastic deep dive today, and it's centered on a tool called AI Media Cutter. Hm. It's an open source project that's, uh, really trying to redefine video editing using AI. It really is. So our mission is to figure out how this thing, this desktop app, uses large language models to turn what is a really complex visual task into something you just do with text. It's a huge shift. We're talking about using LLMs, you know, like Google Gemini or the OpenAI models, to edit based on meaning, on the actual content. Not just pixels on a timeline. Exactly. It moves editing from this highly technical frame-by-frame skill to something that's more, uh, editorial. It's all about the story in the text. And that right there, that changes the whole game for creators. So here's the core of it and what you really need to grasp: text-based editing. Right. It starts with a very high accuracy AI transcription. But the magic, the real trick, is that you suddenly find yourself just editing a document. You see a line you don't like, you delete the sentence. And the video segment that corresponds to it is just gone. It's automatically and precisely cut out of the video file. Which is incredible. What's really fascinating is the efficiency you gain. Yeah. I mean, just think about long form content.",
